// 2.14049329 vs 2.14049294 for ours, and R's fit has nonzero end second derivatives (0.0067, -0.011). Measured
// differences (max |ours - R| / range(y)): nx = 40 with the same df 1e-5 (lambda given: <= 5e-5); n = 200 with
// R's knot subset 2e-5..1e-4; n = 200 with all.knots = TRUE 1.4e-6. R solves trace = df only to ~1e-3 (df = 5 gives
// f$df = 5.000734), so df comparisons use R's achieved f$df. GCV/CV choices: d40 df 6.857188 vs R 6.857174
